# L24 vocabulary: read actions with get? / get_by.
# DSL grammar sources (deps/ash = /Users/sac/ggen_igniter/deps/ash/lib/ash):
#   get?    resource/actions/read.ex:70-76 (boolean, default false; single-result read)
#   get_by  resource/actions/read.ex:83-89 (wrap_list atom; sets get? true, adds an argument
#           and a filter per field)
#   struct  resource/actions/read.ex:12-13, 35-36 (get_by, get? fields)
# Pack action model: legacy aap:Action (resource.ex.tmpl) emits bare `read :name`; L24 reads are
# a separate entity (aap:L24ReadAction) emitted in a Spark fragment <Module>.L24Get, so they
# never redefine an action emitted by resource.ex.tmpl.
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix aap:  <https://ggen.dev/ash-a2a-app#> .

aap:L24ReadAction a owl:Class ; rdfs:comment "Action in the L24 fragment; only actionType read may carry l24Get." .
aap:l24Read       a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:comment "Resource -> L24ReadAction." .
aap:l24Get        a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:comment "true -> get?(true). Legal only when aap:actionType is read AND a key (getByKey or getIdentity) is declared." .
aap:getByKey      a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:comment "Repeatable: one attribute name per triple -> get_by [..]. Must name an aap:attribute of the resource (gate L24_030)." .
aap:getIdentity   a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:comment "Name of an aap:Identity of the resource; its aap:identityKey set becomes the get_by keys." .
